note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/ng/tests/nocaps/gate.om: the no-caps gate of ng (NgNoCaps, 2026-11-11; Drake: "no hard caps on our own
note software ... put a TEST that will alarm"). Handwritten seeded Omega, program mode, Linux AArch64. The child and
note file helpers follow seed/ng/front/gate-front-ir.om; seed/ng/sha256.om supplies sh_dat, sh_all and sh_dig.
note Build: cat seed/ng/sha256.om seed/ng/tests/nocaps/gate.om | seed/out/omc > nocaps-gate
note Run from the repository root: nocaps-gate OMC OMC_SHA256 SCRATCH [NG]
note OMC        the oracle compiler; its sha256 must be OMC_SHA256 (64 lowercase hex) or nothing runs (INVALID)
note SCRATCH    a new directory (created 0700; an existing one is INVALID)
note NG         an ng binary to judge in place of the one this gate builds from seed/ng/ng.units (the negative
note            control: ng from before the no-caps arena must FAIL here); with NG no mutant is built
note 1. Units far past every fixed table ng's front, its ΩIR builder, reader and writer, and its a64 back end had
note    until the no-caps arena (src/ir.om ar_*): each is generated into SCRATCH (u.om, and the same bytes after
note    the mode lines `@ng front-check` and `@ng front-ir`) from the case table g_cs below, never stored.
note 2. Per case NAME WANT OMC KIND: OMC compiles the unit and must exit OMC (0, or a code-generator limit of omc's
note    own, D6: 12); when 0 its binary must exit WANT. ng `@ng front-check` must exit 0, or exactly omc's code
note    with omc's stderr bytes when KIND is d (an om2 diag unit: the stderr records are compared in full). KIND
note    r: ng `@ng front-ir` exits 0, `@ng a64` of its ΩIR exits 0, and that ELF, run, exits WANT. KIND c and d stop
note    after the check. A line per case: ok NAME, the exits, ng's milliseconds per stage and the bytes of the unit.
note 3. Mutants (with no NG): each re-imposes one of the old fixed tables or loop bounds, or breaks the arena's growth, in the
note    composed units of seed/ng/ng.units (pattern FROM present exactly once, replaced by TO); each must make a case
note    fail (KILLED; its own case is tried first). A control: case 1 judged with WANT + 1 must fail.
note 4. The usage alarm (OmcNoCaps's gate-usage, for ng): ng `@ng front-check` of the largest real units in this
note    repository, each after a `usage` line (seed/node/journal-gate.om and ng's own units joined), writes its ng-use
note    record (unit 0 was seed/omc/omc.om until omc declared a run-time pool: ng refuses that as scope, exit 64);
note    the arena top must stay at or below 10% of the arena and every group at or below 5%, and one check at or
note    below 2 s; past a threshold the gate FAILs with ALARM, the number and the threshold. Its control: ng with
note    the arena shrunk to 1048576 words must trip the alarm (with no NG).
note Deadline: every child is killed after 600 s (NOT_RUN, never PASS).
note Output: lines per case, mutant, control and unit, then
note   NOCAPSGATE PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN cases=N fail=F mutants=M killed=K controls=C tripped=T notrun=U
note Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 INVALID, 3 a tool did not build, 4 NOT_RUN. Globals g_*, functions gn_*.
text g_w "seed/ng/ ng.units ng ngm src.om u.om fc.in fi.in ir ai elf bin e0 e1 e2 e3 nul o0 o1 berr us.in seed/node/journal-gate.om uo "
text g_m "FAIL |ok |: omc exit |: omc binary exit |: ng front-check exit |: ng front-ir exit |: ng a64 exit |: program exit |, want |: front-check stderr differs from omc's|NOCAPSGATE PASS|NOCAPSGATE FAIL|NOCAPSGATE INVALID: | cases=| fail=| mutants=| killed=|usage: nocaps-gate OMC OMC_SHA256 SCRATCH [NG]|oracle sha256 differs from OMC_SHA256|scratch exists or cannot be made|build failed: |mutant |: survived every case|: killed by |: pattern not present exactly once|control |: not tripped|: tripped by | ms: check |, ir |, a64 |, elf | (unused)| (unused)| omc=| ng=|NOT_RUN |: a child passed the 600 s deadline| notrun=|: cannot write scratch| bytes=|usage |ALARM |: no ng-use record|: arena top | words, | controls=| tripped=|: front-check took | ms (threshold 2000 ms)|% of the arena (threshold 10%)|NOCAPSGATE NOT_RUN|: group |% of the arena (threshold 5%)| top=| largest=| ms|control usage: arena of 1048576 words|"
text g_pfc "@ng front-check\n"
text g_pfr "@ng front-ir\n"
text g_pa64 "@ng a64\n"
text g_use "usage\n"
note the pieces of the generated units (g_t, separated by |, numbered from 0)
text g_t "|global n| ulong 1\n|fn main to int\nput n0 0 3\nput n99999 0 4\nret int add get n0 0 get n99999 0\nend\n|text t| \"ab\"\n|fn main to int\nx = len t0\ny = len t99999\nret int add x y\nend\n|global long_global_name_| uint 1\n|fn main to int\nput long_global_name_0 0 uint 5\nput long_global_name_99999 0 uint 7\nret int add get long_global_name_0 0 get long_global_name_99999 0\nend\n|fn q| to ulong\nret |\nend\n|fn main to int\na = q0\nb = q59999\nret int rem add a b 256\nend\n|fn inc x ulong to ulong\nret add x 1\nend\nfn main to int\nx = ulong 0\n|x = inc x\n|ret int rem x 256\nend\n|note pppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp\n|fn main to int\nx = int 41\nx = add x 1\nret x\nend\n|fn main to int\nx = ulong 1\n|if eq x 1\n|ret 9\n|end\n|ret 0\nend\n|fn main to int\nx = ulong 0\n|while true\nx = add x 1\nbreak\nend\n|y = ulong 0\nwhile lt y 1\ny = add y 1\nx = add x 1\ncontinue\nend\n|fn main to int\nx = |add |ulong 0| ulong 1|\nret int rem x 256\nend\n|fn inc x ulong to ulong\nret add x 1\nend\nfn main to int\nx = |inc |ulong 0\nret int rem x 256\nend\n|fn main to int\n|a| = new ulong 1 |\n|x = get a9999 0\nret int rem x 256\nend\n|om2\n|fn ia| x int to int inline\nret add x 1\nend\n|om2 diag\nfn main to int\nx = long 0\n|x = add x long 1\n|ret int rem x long 256\nend\n|| \"|aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa|\"\n|fn main to int\nx = len t0\ny = len t16\nret int rem add x y 256\nend\n|abc| x int to int\n|x = ia| x\n|ret x\nend\n|fn main to int\nx = int 0\n|x = fg|ret rem x 256\nend\n|fn inc x ulong to ulong\nret add x 1\nend\n| x ulong to ulong\ny = x\n|y = inc y\n|ret y\nend\n|x = q|neg |long 1\nret int rem x long 256\nend\n|not ||add ulong 1 |fn fg|fn f6 a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong g ulong to ulong\nret add a 1\nend\nfn main to int\nx = |f6 | ulong 1 ulong 1 ulong 1 ulong 1 ulong 1|fn f x long to long\n|x = add x 1\n|ret x\nend\nfn main to int\nret int rem f long 1 256\nend\n|ret x\nend\nfn main to int\nret int rem f long 9223372036854506807 256\nend\n|om2\nfn ia x int to int inline\n|if eq x 1\nret 9\nend\n|ret x\nend\nfn main to int\nx = ia int 41\nret x\nend\n|\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n|fn main to int\nret int rem len t 256\nend\n|"
note the cases: NAME WANT OMC KIND SPEC..., SPEC tokens Lk (piece k), Rk:N (piece k, N times), Nk:m:p:N (for i in
note 0 .. N-1: piece k, i, then piece m and i again when m is not 0, then piece p), I:A:B (the inline-edges unit),
note C:F:K (F functions of K calls each, main calling them all), T:K (K texts of 1 MiB, the last 3 bytes longer).
note KIND r: check, front-ir, a64, the ELF; i: check and front-ir (ng's a64 stage refuses these for a reason named
note below, never a table of the front or the ΩIR); c and d: the check only (d an om2 diag unit, stderr compared).
note Each is past an old fixed table: names100k (front names 8192, front-ir 8192, ΩIR reader 65536 globals, a64
note 65537 addresses), texts100k, long100k (long names 4096), fns60k (functions 4096), calls1m (calls 524288; its
note ΩIR is 21 MB, past the 16 MiB payload and output buffers; one function of 2,000,009 wires is past what a64's
note per-wire tables, 10 words a wire, take in the arena: i), calls1100k (1,100,000 calls in all: a64's 1048576
note call sites), calls524289 (the formerly ngcap row: a64's 262144 wires a function), in64m (input 8 MiB),
note nest5000 (blocks 512, front-ir stack 1024; a64's liveness, blocks x wires / 64 words, is 7,035,471 words a
note bitset, past the arena: i), nest3000 (a64 liveness 2.5 M words, past its 2097152), nest1100 (a function of
note over 1000 blocks: a64 read block 1000 and up as a trap label), breaks3000 / conts3000 (1024 each; a64
note liveness: i), value5000 (value nesting 1024; omc 12), callnest5000, call6nest12000 (front-ir call arguments
note 65536: 72000 here), snap2m (front-ir name snapshots 1048576), arrays10k (front-ir local arrays 8192; omc 12, a64's frame:
note `unsupported`, i), inline22k (inline edges 16384; omc c52e986e and 1e628c80 trapped 3 past 64 inline edges, fixed
note in omc 2495bc25, omega-mv 83507124: omc compiles it and its binary exits 228), diag1m (om2 diag site records 8 MiB), texts17m (ΩIR global
note data 16 MiB, a64 code image 16 MiB), and the deepest value shapes at 32767 levels (d*32767: the stack-derived
note bound of 32768; daddr's right-nested adds need a frame past a64's 4095 bytes: i).
note Old loop bounds of the front and a64 (trap 4 or a64's `unsupported` before the no-caps review): inlrets1m (an
note inline frame's rets walked by fe_inl_pat, 1,000,000 passes: 1,000,001 reachable rets in one inline body called
note once, one inline edge; its front-ir is refused, class 23, by the ΩIR format's 65536 blocks a function, IR.md
note s12: c), text16m (fe_ltxb, a front-ir pass a text byte, 16777216: one literal of 16,777,219 bytes), lalc16m
note (fe_lalc's read-ahead, a pass a blank line and two a statement line, 16777216: 16,777,232 blank lines in main's
note outermost block), fix270k (a64's 262144 branch fixups a function: one overflow branch each), fixtrap270k (the
note same function overflowing: a trap branch patched past the old table, exit 101).
text g_cs "names100k 7 0 r N1:0:2:100000 L3\ntexts100k 4 0 r N4:0:5:100000 L6\nlong100k 12 0 r N7:0:8:100000 L9\nfns60k 95 0 r N10:11:12:60000 L13\ncalls1m 64 0 i L14 R15:1000000 L16\ncalls1100k 224 0 r C:1100:1000\ncalls524289 1 0 r L14 R15:524289 L16\nin64m 42 0 r R17:671088 L18\nnest5000 9 0 i L19 R20:5000 L21 R22:5000 L23\nnest3000 9 0 r L19 R20:3000 L21 R22:3000 L23\nnest1100 9 0 r L19 R20:1100 L21 R22:1100 L23\nbreaks3000 184 0 i L24 R25:3000 L16\nconts3000 184 0 i L24 R26:3000 L16\nvalue5000 136 12 r L27 R28:5000 L29 R30:5000 L31\ncallnest5000 136 0 r L32 R33:5000 L34\ncall6nest12000 224 0 r L70 R71:12000 L29 R72:12000 L31\nsnap2m 9 0 r N1:0:2:1000 L19 R20:2000 L21 R22:2000 L23\narrays10k 15 12 i L35 N36:37:38:10000 L39\ninline22k 228 0 c L40 I:150:150\ndiag1m 0 0 d L43 R44:1000000 L45\ntexts17m 3 0 r T:17\ndneg32767 255 12 r L27 R64:32767 L65\ndadd32767 255 12 r L27 R28:32767 L29 R30:32767 L31\ndcall32767 255 24 r L32 R33:32767 L34\ndnot32767 255 12 r L27 R66:32767 L34\ndaddr32767 255 12 i L27 R68:32767 L34\ninlrets1m 41 0 c L77 R78:1000001 L79\ntext16m 3 0 r L4 L47 R48:1048576 L51 L49 L81\nlalc16m 1 0 r L19 R80:1048577 L16\nfix270k 177 0 r L73 R74:270000 L75\nfixtrap270k 101 0 r L73 R74:270000 L76\n"
global g_wo uint 64
global g_wl uint 64
global g_mo uint 128
global g_ml uint 128
global g_to uint 128
global g_tl uint 128
global g_omc uchar 4096
global g_scr uchar 4096
global g_pa uchar 8192
global g_av uchar 16384
global g_b1 uchar 16777216
global g_b2 uchar 16777216
global g_gb uchar 1048576
global g_gf int 3
global g_o uchar 4096
global g_stb uchar 4
global g_hx uchar 128
global g_ng uchar 4096
global g_mf uchar 256
global g_mt uchar 512
global g_n ulong 48
note g_n: 0 path length, 1 omc length, 2 scratch length (with '/'), 3 argv bytes, 4 argc, 5 b1 length, 6 b2 length,
note 7 generator buffer fill, 8 case cursor in g_cs, 9 out length, 10 cases, 11 failed cases, 12 quiet, 13 current
note case failed (1) or NOT_RUN (2), 14 name start, 15 name end, 16 a child passed the deadline, 17 mutants, 18 killed,
note 19 controls, 20 tripped, 21 NOT_RUN cases, 22 NG given, 23 WANT adjustment (control), 24 spec cursor, 25 spec
note end, 26 unit bytes, 27 mutant FROM length, 28 mutant TO length, 29 ng binary word (2 or 3), 30 alarms,
note 31 last front-check ms, 32 ng-use top, 33 ng-use arena, 34 largest group words, 35 its label start, 36 its end

note ---- words and output -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gn_split t ulong to void
w = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
if eq t 0
for i ulong len g_w bound 4096
if eq get g_w i 32
put g_wo w uint s
put g_wl w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
end
if eq t 1
for i ulong len g_m bound 8192
if eq get g_m i 124
put g_mo w uint s
put g_ml w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
end
if eq t 2
for i ulong len g_t bound 65536
if eq get g_t i 124
put g_to w uint s
put g_tl w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
end
end
fn gn_init to void
gn_split 0
gn_split 1
gn_split 2
put g_n 29 2
end
fn gn_c b ulong to void
n = get g_n 9
if lt n len g_o
put g_o n uchar b
put g_n 9 add n 1
end
end
fn gn_nl to void
gn_c 10
r = write 1 g_o 0 get g_n 9
put g_n 9 0
end
fn gn_say i ulong to void
s = ulong get g_mo i
for j ulong ulong get g_ml i bound 256
gn_c ulong get g_m add s j
end
end
fn gn_num v ulong to void
if ge v 10
gn_num div v 10
end
gn_c add 48 rem v 10
end
fn gn_name to void
for p ulong sub get g_n 15 get g_n 14 bound 256
gn_c ulong get g_cs add get g_n 14 p
end
end
note a failure of the current case (FAIL NAME<message i>), unless quiet
fn gn_fail i ulong to void
put g_n 13 1
if eq get g_n 12 0
gn_say 0
gn_name
gn_say i
end
end
fn gn_failv i ulong v ulong w ulong to void
gn_fail i
if eq get g_n 12 0
gn_num v
gn_say 8
gn_num w
gn_nl
end
end

note ---- paths and files ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gn_pclr to void
put g_n 0 0
end
fn gn_pc c ulong to void
n = get g_n 0
if lt n len g_pa
put g_pa n uchar c
put g_n 0 add n 1
end
end
fn gn_pw i ulong to void
s = ulong get g_wo i
for j ulong ulong get g_wl i bound 64
gn_pc ulong get g_w add s j
end
end
note scratch file word i
fn gn_ps i ulong to void
gn_pclr
for j ulong get g_n 2 bound 4096
gn_pc ulong get g_scr j
end
gn_pw i
end
fn gn_open fl ulong to int
r = fopen g_pa 0 get g_n 0 int fl 420
if lt r 0
ret -1
end
ret int r
end
fn gn_rdonly to int
ret gn_open 524288
end
fn gn_wronly to int
ret gn_open 524865
end
fn gn_exe to int
r = unlink g_pa 0 get g_n 0
x = fopen g_pa 0 get g_n 0 524865 493
if lt x 0
ret -1
end
ret int x
end
fn gn_fclo fd int to void
if ge fd 0
r = fclose fd
end
end
note write b1[0, n) to fd; false on a short write
fn gn_wr fd int n ulong to bool
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 16777217
x = write fd g_b1 o sub n o
if le x 0
ret false
end
o = add o ulong x
end
ret true
end
note read the file at g_pa into b1 at offset o; its length, or 2^63 when unreadable or too big
fn gn_slurp o ulong to ulong
fd = gn_rdonly
if lt fd 0
ret shl ulong 1 63
end
n = o
ok = true
while true bound 16777218
x = read fd g_b1 n sub len g_b1 n
if lt x 0
ok = false
break
end
if eq x 0
break
end
n = add n ulong x
if ge n len g_b1
ok = false
break
end
end
gn_fclo fd
if not ok
ret shl ulong 1 63
end
ret sub n o
end
note read up to m bytes of fd into b1 (k 1) or b2 (k 2); the count (0 at the end)
fn gn_rdn fd int k ulong m ulong to ulong
n = ulong 0
while lt n m bound 1048577
x = long 0
if eq k 1
x = read fd g_b1 n sub m n
else
x = read fd g_b2 n sub m n
end
if le x 0
ret n
end
n = add n ulong x
end
ret n
end
fn gn_eqn n ulong to bool
for j ulong n bound 1048576
if ne get g_b1 j get g_b2 j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note the scratch files w1 and w2 hold the same bytes
fn gn_fcmp w1 ulong w2 ulong to bool
gn_ps w1
f1 = gn_rdonly
gn_ps w2
f2 = gn_rdonly
ok = and ge f1 0 ge f2 0
dn = false
while and ok not dn bound 65536
a = gn_rdn f1 1 1048576
b = gn_rdn f2 2 1048576
if ne a b
ok = false
else
if eq a 0
dn = true
end
ok = gn_eqn a
end
end
gn_fclo f1
gn_fclo f2
ret ok
end
note scratch file d = the mode line text m (0 a64, 1 front-check) then the bytes of scratch file s
fn gn_pref m ulong s ulong d ulong to bool
n = ulong 0
if eq m 0
n = len g_pa64
for j ulong n bound 64
put g_b1 j get g_pa64 j
end
else
n = len g_use
for j ulong n bound 64
put g_b1 j get g_use j
end
end
gn_ps d
fo = gn_wronly
if lt fo 0
ret false
end
ok = gn_wr fo n
if eq m 2
ok = and ok gn_wr fo 0
end
gn_ps s
fi = gn_rdonly
dn = false
while and ok not dn bound 65536
if lt fi 0
ok = false
else
k = gn_rdn fi 1 1048576
if eq k 0
dn = true
else
ok = gn_wr fo k
end
end
end
gn_fclo fi
gn_fclo fo
ret ok
end

note ---- children ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gn_aclr to void
put g_n 3 2
put g_n 4 0
end
fn gn_apa to void
p = get g_n 3
n = get g_n 0
for j ulong n bound 8192
put g_av add add p 2 j get g_pa j
end
put g_av p uchar and n 255
put g_av add p 1 uchar shr n 8
put g_n 3 add p add n 2
c = add get g_n 4 1
put g_n 4 c
put g_av 0 uchar and c 255
put g_av 1 uchar shr c 8
end
fn gn_redir s int d int to void
if ne dupfd s d 0 long d
exit 127
end
end
note run the argument list with stdin, stdout, stderr fds (closed here); the exit code, 256 + the signal, 1000
note when the child passed the 600 s deadline (killed; g_n 16 = 1)
fn gn_spawn fi int fo int fe int to ulong
if or lt fi 0 or lt fo 0 lt fe 0
gn_fclo fi
gn_fclo fo
gn_fclo fe
ret 512
end
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
exit 2
end
if eq pid 0
gn_redir fi 0
gn_redir fo 1
gn_redir fe 2
r = execprog g_av 0 get g_n 3
exit 127
end
gn_fclo fi
gn_fclo fo
gn_fclo fe
t0 = monons
while true bound 1000000000
r = waitpid int pid g_stb 0 len g_stb 1
if eq r pid
x = ulong get g_stb 0
if ne x 0
ret add 256 x
end
ret ulong get g_stb 1
end
if lt r 0
exit 2
end
if gt sub monons t0 600000000000
r = killpid int pid 9
r = waitpid int pid g_stb 0 len g_stb 0
put g_n 16 1
ret 1000
end
q = sleepns 200000
end
exit 2
end
note run scratch program p with stdin scratch i, stdout scratch o (an executable when ex), stderr scratch e
fn gn_run p ulong i ulong o ulong ex bool e ulong to ulong
gn_ps i
fi = gn_rdonly
gn_aclr
gn_ps p
gn_apa
gn_ps o
fo = int -1
if ex
fo = gn_exe
else
fo = gn_wronly
end
gn_ps e
fe = gn_wronly
ret gn_spawn fi fo fe
end
note OMC with stdin scratch i, stdout scratch o (an executable), stderr scratch e
fn gn_omc i ulong o ulong e ulong to ulong
gn_ps i
fi = gn_rdonly
gn_aclr
gn_pclr
for j ulong get g_n 1 bound 4096
gn_pc ulong get g_omc j
end
gn_apa
gn_ps o
fo = gn_exe
gn_ps e
fe = gn_wronly
ret gn_spawn fi fo fe
end
note milliseconds since t0
fn gn_ms t0 long to ulong
ret ulong div sub monons t0 1000000
end

note ---- the generator ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note g_gb is flushed to the g_gf files (u.om, fc.in, fi.in) when full and at the end
fn gn_gflush to bool
n = get g_n 7
ok = true
for f ulong 3
fd = get g_gf f
o = ulong 0
while and ok lt o n bound 1048577
x = write fd g_gb o sub n o
if le x 0
ok = false
else
o = add o ulong x
end
end
end
put g_n 26 add get g_n 26 n
put g_n 7 0
ret ok
end
fn gn_gc c ulong to void
n = get g_n 7
if ge n len g_gb
z = gn_gflush
n = ulong 0
end
put g_gb n uchar c
put g_n 7 add n 1
end
fn gn_gt k ulong to void
s = ulong get g_to k
for j ulong ulong get g_tl k bound 4096
gn_gc ulong get g_t add s j
end
end
fn gn_gn v ulong to void
if ge v 10
gn_gn div v 10
end
gn_gc add 48 rem v 10
end
note the next decimal number of the spec at g_n 24 (stops at ':', ' ' or the end of the line)
fn gn_snum to ulong
v = ulong 0
p = get g_n 24
while lt p get g_n 25 bound 32
c = ulong get g_cs p
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
put g_n 24 add p 1
ret v
end
v = add mul v 10 sub c 48
p = add p 1
end
put g_n 24 p
ret v
end
note the inline-edges unit (I:A:B): A inline functions ia0.., B functions f0.. each calling every inline function on
note x, main calling every f on x: B * A edges from a function to an inline function, each recorded once
fn gn_ginl a ulong b ulong to void
for k ulong a bound 100000
gn_gt 41
gn_gn k
gn_gt 42
end
for j ulong b bound 100000
gn_gt 69
gn_gn j
gn_gt 52
for k ulong a bound 100000
gn_gt 53
gn_gn k
gn_gt 54
end
gn_gt 55
end
gn_gt 56
for j ulong b bound 100000
gn_gt 57
gn_gn j
gn_gt 54
end
gn_gt 58
end
note the spread-calls unit (C:F:K): F functions q0.. of K calls each, main calling every q on x
fn gn_gcall f ulong k ulong to void
gn_gt 59
for j ulong f bound 100000
gn_gt 10
gn_gn j
gn_gt 60
for i ulong k bound 100000
gn_gt 61
